    <name>
      <text>Chain rule_ Question 3</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given the following,</p>

<p>\(\qquad \displaystyle z={@func_z@}\)</p>
<p>\(\qquad  \displaystyle y={@func_y@} \)</p>

<p> We can use Chain Rule to compute \(\displaystyle \frac{dz}{dx}\) from the following steps; </p>

<p>Recall the formula for the Chain Rule \(\displaystyle \frac{dz}{dx} = \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{x}} + \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{y}}\frac{dy}{dx}, \)</p>

<p> \(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{x}} = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{y}}= \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{dy}{dx}= \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]] </p>
<p> \(\displaystyle \frac{dz}{dx} =  \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]] </p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{dz}{dx} = \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{x}} + \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{y}}\frac{dy}{dx} \)</p>
<p> \(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{x}} = {@func1@}\) </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{y}}={@func2a@} \) </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{dy}{dx}={@func2b@}\) </p>
<p>   \(\displaystyle \quad = {@func1@}+({@func2a*func2b@}) \)</p>
<p>   \(\quad = {@ta@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
